{"id":2268008,"name":"Realistic Snapshot (Z-Image-Turbo + Krea 2)","description":"<p>💎 <span style=\"color:rgb(255, 255, 255)\"><strong>PREMIUM WORKFLOW — GET THE FULL PACKAGE HERE</strong></span><strong>:</strong><br />👉 <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"ugc\" href=\"https://monkeyforever.gumroad.com/l/max-realism-kit\"><strong>https://monkeyforever.gumroad.com/l/max-realism-kit</strong></a> 👈</p><p>💬 <strong>Discord (community, 2.000+ members):</strong> <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"ugc\" href=\"https://discord.gg/GQhYhqDrC3\"><strong>discord.gg/GQhYhqDrC3</strong></a></p><p></p><p>This LoRA is just the start. The <span style=\"color:rgb(255, 255, 255)\"><strong>Max Realism Kit</strong></span><strong> </strong>is the complete pre-configured system I use for every image you see on this page, load it, drop in your prompt, hit queue. Zero setup guessing:</p><p>🎛️ <strong>Two premium ComfyUI workflows</strong> with a custom sampler built from scratch, everything pre-set and pre-tuned, no node fiddling<br />👥 <strong>Multi-LoRA stacking that actually works</strong> - character + realism combined without one killing the other. No plastic skin, no washed-out identity<br />🔞 <strong>Full NSFW support</strong> with dedicated detailing<br />✍️ <strong>LoRA Caption Studio </strong> - build and caption your own AI influencer dataset<br />📕 <strong>19-page guide</strong> - from zero to a finished character LoRA<br />🔄 <strong>Pay once, own forever</strong> - free lifetime updates (already on V1.6), Krea 2 workflow coming to owners first.</p><p><strong>300+ customers.</strong> Instant delivery. ⚡</p><p></p><h3 id=\"version-breakdown\">Version Breakdown</h3><p><strong>v1.0:</strong> The foundation of the project. It excels at adding a base layer of realism and texture to your images. Trained on a smaller dataset, it is lightweight and perfect for enhancing simple, straightforward compositions with a natural touch.</p><p><strong>v2.0:</strong> A specialized, experimental step focused on the \"camera roll\" aesthetic. This version is highly effective for generating raw, unpolished amateur snapshots and candid moments. Note: It can be slightly unstable/temperamental but produces unique, gritty results when it hits.</p><p><strong>v3.0:</strong> The best offering of the previous cycle. Trained on a vastly expanded and refined dataset, V3 delivers peak photorealism. It strikes the perfect balance, offering the raw, \"in-the-moment\" vibe of amateur shots alongside the high-fidelity details required for professional-looking images.</p><p><strong>v3.5 Photorealism:</strong> A massive leap in optical correctness. It understands the physics of light passing through skin (subsurface scattering), reflections on wet surfaces (specular highlights), and lens distortions (chromatic aberration). It handles complex scenarios like mirror selfies and underwater refraction with ease.</p><p><strong>🚀 v5.0 (Real Life Version): </strong>The Massive Update This is the most comprehensive update yet, trained on a significantly larger dataset with 100+ new high-fidelity images and captions. v5 is designed to drastically reduce artifacts and \"weird\" AI hallucinations while enhancing anatomical precision and lighting physics.<br /><br /><strong>✨ Krea 2 (Experimental)</strong>: The first port to a brand-new base model. Retrained from the ground up on a 600-image dataset (double the v5 set), now leaning heavily on modern iPhone photos and a much larger NSFW spread—replacing the early-2000s amateur shots that weighed down the older data. Same signature style as v5, just cleaner, more versatile, and better balanced. Krea 2 behaves very differently from Z-Image-Turbo: prompt adherence is significantly better, though Z-Image still edges it out on raw style and realism. This version also shines at enhancing and boosting detail. Still experimental and being actively refined—I recommend pushing strength to 1.5, sometimes even 2.0, depending on the image. Don't expect old prompts or workflows to carry over.</p><p></p><hr /><h3 id=\"usage-tips\">💡 Usage Tips</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Recommended Strength:</strong> <strong>0.60 - 0.70</strong> (This version is potent; start lower and adjust up if needed).</p></li><li><p><strong>Trigger Words:</strong> While not strictly required, using these tags will force the model to activate specific textures and lighting styles: <br /><br /><em>For the \"Camera Roll\" Look:</em> <code>amateur digital snapshot</code>, <code>candid</code>, <code>smartphone capture</code>, <code>high ISO noise</code>, <code>direct on-camera flash</code>.<br /><em>For High-Fidelity Details:</em> <code>visible pores</code>, <code>visible vellus hair</code>, <code>subsurface scattering</code>, <code>detailed skin texture</code>.<br /><em>For Optical Realism:</em> <code>wide-angle lens</code>, <code>barrel distortion</code>, <code>chromatic aberration</code>, <code>depth of field</code>.</p></li></ul><p></p>","allowNoCredit":true,"allowCommercialUse":["Image","RentCivit","Rent","Sell"],"allowDerivatives":true,"allowDifferentLicense":true,"type":"LORA","minor":false,"sfwOnly":false,"poi":false,"nsfw":false,"nsfwLevel":15,"availability":"Public","userId":2867257,"baseModels":["Krea 2","ZImageTurbo"],"cosmetic":null,"supportsGeneration":true,"stats":{"downloadCount":63080,"thumbsUpCount":2913,"thumbsDownCount":11,"commentCount":84,"tippedAmountCount":700},"creator":{"username":"MonkeyForever","image":"https://image.civitai.com/xG1nkqKTMzGDvpLrqFT7WA/f1a27bd8-71ba-459e-8869-d95d765fd2a0/width=96/MonkeyForever.jpeg"},"tags":["digicam","photorealistic","2000s","photography","amateur","realism","candid","style","beautifulgirl","ethereal","amateurphoto","influencer","selfie"],"modelVersions":[{"id":3084537,"index":0,"name":"Krea2 (v0.5)","baseModel":"Krea 2","baseModelType":"Standard","createdAt":"2026-06-30T11:23:38.863Z","publishedAt":"2026-07-03T17:24:11.641Z","status":"Published","flags":0,"availability":"Public","nsfwLevel":15,"description":"<p><strong>Realistic Snapshot - Krea 2 (v0.5)</strong></p><p>This is the Krea 2 port of Realistic Snapshot, retrained from the ground up on a 600-image dataset (up from 300 on the Z-Image-Turbo v5 release). Same casual smartphone-photography aesthetic, now adapted for Krea 2.</p><p><strong>What changed in the dataset:</strong> This time the set leans more on modern iPhone photos and includes a lot more NSFW material. The v5 Z-Image-Turbo dataset had way too many early-2000s amateur shots dragging the look in that direction. The core style is still the same as v5, just cleaner, more versatile, and better balanced.</p><p><strong>Heads up. This one is experimental.</strong> Krea 2 is still a new model and I'm honestly still figuring out how to prompt it consistently. It behaves very differently from Z-Image-Turbo, so don't expect your old prompts or workflows to carry over. Results can vary a lot.</p><p><strong>Strength:</strong> Default 1.0 is a starting point, but I'd recommend pushing higher, 1.5, sometimes even 2.0 depending on the image. Krea 2 takes the LoRA differently than Z-Image did, so feel free to experiment past the usual range.</p><p><strong>What it does well:</strong> Beyond the snapshot look, this LoRA is great at enhancing and boosting detail in images, you can see it clearly in the showcase. The detail enhancement is one of the stronger surprises here.</p>","covered":true,"stats":{"downloadCount":17776,"thumbsUpCount":843,"thumbsDownCount":0},"files":[{"id":2963911,"sizeKB":223230.1953125,"name":"RealisticSnapshotKrea2.safetensors","overrideName":null,"type":"Model","pickleScanResult":"Success","pickleScanMessage":null,"virusScanResult":"Success","virusScanMessage":null,"scannedAt":"2026-06-30T11:27:09.235Z","metadata":{"format":"SafeTensor","fp":"bf16","isRequired":false},"hashes":{"AutoV1":"781A934D","AutoV2":"DFD67EB881","SHA256":"DFD67EB881BEC4CAEB9409E5B7C127ADCB9FB724E6007E1E77165AF51E6F908D","CRC32":"60D769ED","BLAKE3":"13115D2DFCAB2F149D4FC